# Svelte components

A `.sveltex` file is still a Svelte component. You can drop real components
straight into the Markdown, and they stay fully interactive after hydration.

## An interactive island

Here is a `Counter` component — click it:

<Counter />

It is defined in `src/lib/Counter.svelte` and uses Svelte 5 runes.

## Components that wrap Markdown

The `Callout` component receives Markdown as its children: SvelTeX processes
the content *inside* the tags before handing it over.

<Callout type="tip">
This text is **Markdown**, rendered inside a Svelte component — it can hold
`inline code` and [links](https://svelte.dev).
</Callout>

<Callout type="warning">
Each callout takes a `type` prop, so the same component renders several styles.
</Callout>

## Verbatim environments

The `Verb` environment is configured to *escape* its contents, so
HTML-special characters and curly braces survive untouched instead of being
parsed as markup or Svelte interpolation:

<Verb>
This is verbatim: <strong>literal tags</strong>, the comparison 1 < 2, and
{curly braces} all survive.
</Verb>
